n absence receipts.\"\n    },\n    \"cleanup\": {\n      \"measurementClientExitCode\": 0,\n      \"primarySqlExitCode\": 0,\n      \"secondarySqlExitCode\": 0,\n      \"controllerExitCode\": 1,\n      \"rawCleanup\": \"failed_or_unknown_preserved_evidence\",\n      \"immediateCapacityCriterionPassed\": false,\n      \"ownedResourceAndPathAbsenceVerified\": true,\n      \"laterSameCapacityCriterionPassed\": true,\n      \"capacityCriterionBytes\": 1073741824,\n      \"laterDeficitFromBeforeBytes\": 270692352,\n      \"detail\": \"All724 recorded commands terminated0 without recorded timeout or forced termination. Both SQL terminal logs contain setup=0 sql=0 and shutdown evidence. Guarded guest unlink and runtime inventories establish logical absence. Later capacity evidence binds the unchanged raw\/canonical hashes and uses the original1GiB criterion. Postrun audit\/report changes preserve controller1 and the immediate failure; they do not alter runtime SOURCE or measurements. Capacity recovery does not establish physical block erasure or global cache purge.\"\n    },\n    \"limitations\": [\n      \"Unsupported Linux amd64 through Rosetta; no native-performance conversion or product ranking.\",\n      \"Fixed case order, cache history, compilation, host IO\/thermal conditions and the additional A instance prevent causal isolation of state effects.\",\n      \"Three samples per cell provide descriptive statistics only.\",\n      \"Quiet static fixture; service budget remains UNAVAILABLE.\",\n      \"Sch-S and CPU\/IO\/version-retention costs remain; sparse observations do not establish absence of every short-lived lock.\",\n      \"No generalization to TDE, LOB, compression, arbitrary100-column schemas, HA or failover.\",\n      \"Aggregate acceptance and commit\/push verification remain separate from this independent engineer review.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"reviewEvidence\": {\n    \"ownerProof\": {\n      \"path\": \"results\/reviews\/sqlserver-manual-count-100m\/owne